## What you get

A tokio service with two tasks: BLE (`scan → connect → subscribe → reconnect with backoff`) and a Cinnamon StatusNotifierItem tray (`ksni` 0.3, same pattern as voxtype). They talk over a `watch` channel so the tray never blocks the radio.

BLE uses **`bluer` 0.17** (official BlueZ bindings) instead of btleplug so we take `Session::default_adapter()` — on this box that is `hci0`, the Broadcom stick that can see the sensor. Justification is in `README.md`.

## Build

`cargo build --release` succeeded. Binary: `target/release/inkbird-tray`.

```bash
./target/release/inkbird-tray
```

## Live run (~3 minutes on the real device)

Used default adapter `hci0` (`XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX`), rediscovered `Ink@IAM-T1` at `XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX` by name/manufacturer fingerprint (MAC not hard-coded), subscribed to `ffe4`, and decoded three DATA packets:

```
DATA 55aa01101002ea027602a903da0100fd | CO2 681 ppm | 74.6 °F | 23.7 °C | RH 63.0 % | 986 hPa
DATA 55aa01101002ea0280029b03da0100f9 | CO2 667 ppm | 74.6 °F | 23.7 °C | RH 64.0 % | 986 hPa
DATA 55aa01101002ec0280029703da0100f7 | CO2 663 ppm | 74.8 °F | 23.8 °C | RH 64.0 % | 986 hPa
```

CSV at `~/.local/share/inkbird-tray/readings.csv`:

```
timestamp,co2_ppm,temp,unit,temp_c,humidity_pct,pressure_hpa
2026-08-14T13:43:00,681,74.6,F,23.67,63.0,986
2026-08-14T13:45:00,667,74.6,F,23.67,64.0,986
2026-08-14T13:46:00,663,74.8,F,23.78,64.0,986
```

SIGTERM disconnected the sensor and exited cleanly (`shutdown: disconnecting` → `stopped`).

## Tray on this session bus

`xapp-sn-watcher` was already owning `org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher`. After start:

| evidence | value |
| --- | --- |
| log | `system tray icon started (StatusNotifierItem id=inkbird-tray)` |
| well-known name | `org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-261877-1` owned by pid 261877 `inkbird-tray` |
| watcher list | `RegisteredStatusNotifierItems` included `org.kde.StatusNotifierItem-261877-1/StatusNotifierItem` |

After SIGTERM that name was gone. I did not visually confirm the Cinnamon icon; the registration path ran without panicking.

Icons (all present in Mint-X): `weather-clear` / `weather-few-clouds` / `weather-storm` by CO₂; `view-refresh`, `bluetooth-active`, `bluetooth`, `dialog-warning`, `network-offline`, `dialog-error` for the other states.

## Also shipped

- `inkbird-tray.service` — `Type=simple`, `Restart=always`, `RestartSec=10`, `After=bluetooth.target`, `WantedBy=default.target`. Not installed.
- `README.md` — build/run, protocol, tray icons, phone-app / BLE-switch troubleshooting.
- 7 unit tests on the live-capture decode (`55aa0110…` → 73.5 °F / 61 % / 781 ppm / 986 hPa).
